{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>When they warm up</b> — as when they cool down, according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory, because of מזדרבבי." "<b>They are knotted</b> — they bind together. Likewise from their words, in their saying צומת הגידין, and it is the place where they were joined. And the meaning: even though they are in this strength." "<b>When they are hot</b> — when the heat comes, it is as though they vanished from their place and were never there, from ידך נרו (your lamp), whose sense is a word of extinguishing and consumption. And what seems right to me: that this verse is doubled in meaning, in the manner of the verses of this book and other books, and the sense of יזורבו is 'they grow hot,' and it has no parallel." "And the interpretation of <b>they are knotted</b> — they are cut off, like: יצמיתם HaShem (may HaShem exterminate them)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The comment is cryptic and possibly textually corrupt; יזורבו is read as 'they warm up' and contrasted with 'they cool down,' while מזדרבבי (Aramaic) is left untranslated as Ibn Ezra cites it.", 1 "The phrase צומת הגידין is left in Hebrew as Ibn Ezra's cited rabbinic source.", 2 "Resolved the partial verse citation ידך נרו as a biblical allusion; the reference is uncertain as Ibn Ezra quotes only two words."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:02.511253638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}